WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.840
Hey, how you doing?

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:01.660
I'm Eddie.

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:02.760
Nice to meet you.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:06.640
The question is, immigration is good for America, right?

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.480
Overall.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.740
If you look at the net positives to things like

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.280
our society, our culture, our food, our economy,

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.120
our general diversity.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.639
I know the D word is a bad word in places like this.

00:00:17.639 --> 00:00:19.240
I think immigrants have been a net positive.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.520
I think if you look at your everyday lives,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.120
we all benefit from immigration.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.280
And what kind of conservatives disagree with that?

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.360
The guys, some of the guys who told me to leave this place

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.440
and go back to, you know, I'm not a citizen.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.719
Do you think all conservatives?

00:00:30.719 --> 00:00:31.540
No.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.639
No, in fact, Ronald Reagan, who is a president

00:00:33.639 --> 00:00:35.439
I wasn't a big fan of until Donald Trump came along.

00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:37.439
Now people like Reagan look good in comparison.

00:00:37.439 --> 00:00:40.680
Reagan said in 1986, our country is a nation of immigrants.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.360
Our immigrant heritage is our strength.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.200
He gave an amnesty to 3 million undocumented migrants.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.040
He understood the value of immigration.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.279
So I'm with Reagan.

00:00:48.279 --> 00:00:50.360
Although this guy is putting his thumb down there.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.080
So Reagan's not popular in right wing crowds these days.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:54.200
Well, he's popular with me.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.040
Good to hear.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:57.520
I'm a deferred action of childhood arrivals.

00:00:57.759 --> 00:01:00.720
Actually, I was an illegal immigrant myself.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.060
I came here when I was 10.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:04.599
I'm what you would call a legal alien now.

00:01:04.599 --> 00:01:09.599
I didn't have any say on my parents, you know, choices.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:10.559
Yes.

00:01:10.559 --> 00:01:12.320
Do I think that they were well-meaning

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.400
by wanting to bring me over for a better future?

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.400
Absolutely.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.239
I believe that.

00:01:18.239 --> 00:01:19.059
Yeah.

00:01:19.059 --> 00:01:20.440
Did they break law?

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.260
Yes.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.160
Do I agree with people breaking the law?

